{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1403971-lugh-the-irish-god","id":1403971,"title":"Lugh, the Irish God","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-22T03:56:28-07:00","id":1403971,"title":"Lugh, the Irish God","content":"Good day,<br /> I m going to start GMing a chronicle set in arthurian britannia.<br /> The main antagonist and Keeper of the three changeling player should be modeled after the god Lugh, and without a published example of a 2 ed true fae &quot;sheet&quot; i m encountering some difficulties in creating it, and also i m not an expert of celtic mythology.<br /> So i m asking for help to anyone who wish to collaborate.<br /> <br /> The project will be multi staged.<br /> In stage 1 i need to define the true name and the 3 associated titles, including the seeming more in tune with them.<br /> In stage 2 i need to define each title tells and regalia,<br /> and the other minor details like the shapes that each title can assume.<br /> In stage 3 i need to define the frailties and weak points of each title oaths, giving player a better chance to confront with the entity and good story hooks.<br /> <br /> It s a lot of work and i will be much grateful for any help or advice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T03:57:51-07:00","id":1403973,"title":"","content":"For more info on Lugh, i ve found this very useful article<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.imbas.org/articles/lugus.html#12\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.imbas.org/articles/lugus.html#12\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.imbas.org/articles/lugus.html#12\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.imbas.org/articles/lugus.html#12 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T04:02:50-07:00","id":1403975,"title":"","content":"For the three titles i would use Lugh classical epitheth, like<br /> -L\u00e1mfada, \u201cOf the Long Arm&quot; (fairest? Associated with the spear of command?)<br /> -Ild\u00e1nach (the Skilled God) (wizened?)<br /> -Lonnb\u00e9imnech &quot;the Fierce Striker&quot; (elemental? associated with thunder?)<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T04:04:08-07:00","id":1403976,"title":"","content":"I still need to learn 2nd ed Changeling.<br /> <br /> But Lleu Llaw Gyffes is the nephew of Gwydion and is a Welsh version of Lugh, so that is another angle to tap into for Lugh inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T04:44:05-07:00","id":1465620,"title":"","content":"Here is the first prototype at last!<br /> Let me know what do you think about it and most importantly if this structure can represent a 2 edition True fae<br /> <br /> <br /> Lugh<br /> Wyrd 8 <br /> <br /> Titles<br /> It possess 3 &quot;twin titles&quot;<br /> Each one can manifest as an Actor at the same time, but not in the same place.<br /> If the need arise, all three can combine in a three faced body.<br /> The combined form still has one action per turn, but uses the best stats of all of the Titles, and health and glamour loss are distributed evenly beetween the three pools.<br /> Only one Title can enter the material world at any given time. <br /> <br /> -L\u00e1mfada, \u201cOf the Long Arm&quot; <br /> fairest<br /> Tell <br /> Mistletoe, usually as a crown<br /> Regalia<br /> Crown (The peak of Tara, the stone of destiny)<br /> Sword (The sword Freagartach)<br /> Jewel (His wife Nas, a very loyal changeling)<br /> Steed (The horse Enbarr) <br /> <br /> -Ild\u00e1nach (the Skilled God) <br /> wizened<br /> Tell <br /> Corrbolg, a bag full of treasures<br /> Regalia<br /> Crown (The Golden fields of Tara, bountiful of crops)<br /> Sword (The Tathlum, projectile of his sling)<br /> Jewel (His Silver harp encrusted with gems, which is also a former changeling wife)<br /> Steed (A flock of Ravens, with black and white feathers)<br /> <br /> <br /> -Lonnb\u00e9imnech &quot;the Fierce Striker&quot; <br /> elemental thunder<br /> Tell <br /> Sound of roaring thunder even with clear sky<br /> Regalia<br /> Crown (The perpetual clouds above Tara)<br /> Sword (The spear Assal)<br /> Jewel (His Forge on Tara)<br /> Steed (The hound Failinis) <br /> <br /> The True name is the moan of a virgin man on his first climax<br /> It is linked to bestial things, darkness and euphory, akin to a Satyr<br /> Does the True name need a sheet with Seeming, Tell, Regalia and Frailties or It manifests only if stripped of all its Titles ? <br /> <br /> Also i have difficulties in creating Frailties associated to the legend of Lugh, any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}